Cant install gdm because conflicts with file gdm 1:2.22.0-1
May 22

This is the classic GDM conflict on RHEL 9 — an old GDM package from a non-standard repo (likely a leftover from a failed install or third-party source) is blocking the current one. The version 1:2.22.0-1 is ancient (GNOME 2 era, circa 2008) which means it came from somewhere other than RHEL 9's repos.

Diagnose first:
bash

rpm -qi gdm
# Shows what installed it, from which repo, and when

rpm -qf /path/to/conflicting/file
# Replace with the actual file path from the conflict error

dnf repoquery --installed gdm
# Shows epoch:version:release and repo origin

Check what's actually owning the conflict:
bash

# Paste your exact error to get the file path, then:
rpm -qf /usr/share/gdm/greeter/autostart/gnome-settings-daemon.desktop
# (or whatever file the conflict named)

Fix — force-remove the ghost package then reinstall:
bash

# Option 1: dnf handles it
dnf remove gdm
dnf install gdm

# Option 2: if dnf remove itself fails due to deps
rpm -e --nodeps gdm
dnf install gdm

# Option 3: if the epoch is the problem (1: prefix means epoch 1)
dnf install --allowerasing gdm

The --allowerasing flag is the key one here — it tells dnf it's allowed to remove conflicting packages to satisfy the install. This is the standard fix when an epoch mismatch is blocking resolution.

If it came from an EPEL or third-party repo:
bash

dnf repolist all
dnf repoquery --installed --qf "%{name} %{version} %{repoid}" gdm

If the repoid shows something other than rhel-9-* or appstream, that's your culprit repo. Disable it and retry:
bash

dnf install gdm --disablerepo=<bad-repo-name>

Post the exact conflict error text if none of these clear it — the specific file path in the conflict message points directly at what's holding it.

