That's a different issue — not a missing file, it's a missing generated header. efitools generates KEK.auth, DB.auth, and PK.auth during the build as compiled-in demo keys, and the header that declares those arrays hasn't been created yet when LockDown.c tries to include them.

This means the build targets are running out of order, usually because a prior make step failed silently or the generated files are missing from a partial build.

Fix — clean everything and rebuild with the key generation step forced first:
bash

cd efitools

# Full clean
make clean

# Check if you have all the tools needed to generate the keys
which openssl
which cert-to-efi-sig-list
which sign-efi-sig-list

# cert-to-efi-sig-list and sign-efi-sig-list come FROM efitools itself
# which creates a chicken-and-egg problem — fix by building in stages

The chicken-and-egg is the real issue here. efitools needs its own tools to generate the signed key headers it compiles into LockDown.efi, but those tools aren't built yet on a clean system.

The staged build that breaks the cycle:
bash

# Stage 1 — build only the host-side tools (pure C, no EFI, no keys needed)
make cert-to-efi-sig-list sign-efi-sig-list \
     hash-to-efi-sig-list sig-list-to-certs \
     cert-to-efi-hash-list efi-readvar efi-updatevar

# Stage 2 — now generate the demo keys using the tools you just built
make PK.auth KEK.auth DB.auth

# Stage 3 — now build the EFI binaries that need those headers
make GNUEFIDIR=/usr/lib/gnuefi

# Stage 4 — install
make install

If Stage 1 itself fails because cert-to-efi-sig-list etc. are not valid individual targets:
bash

# Tell make to skip the EFI/LockDown targets entirely
make GNUEFIDIR=/usr/lib/gnuefi \
  TARGETS="efi-updatevar efi-readvar sign-efi-sig-list \
           cert-to-efi-sig-list sig-list-to-certs \
           hash-to-efi-sig-list cert-to-efi-hash-list"

If that syntax isn't supported by the Makefile, the nuclear clean option:
bash

# Check if openssl can generate the keys manually to unblock the build
openssl req -new -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -noenc \
  -keyout PK.key -out PK.crt \
  -days 3650 -subj "/CN=efitools build PK/"

# Then let make use them
make GNUEFIDIR=/usr/lib/gnuefi PK.crt KEK.crt db.crt
make GNUEFIDIR=/usr/lib/gnuefi

Paste the first few lines of make clean output and the exact first error line from the fresh make attempt — that'll confirm whether it's the stage ordering or a missing dep earlier in the chain.

