unit_address_vs_reg — node has a unit address in its name (@3a000000) but no matching reg property, or vice versa. Cosmetic only, hardware still initializes.

pci_device_reg / pci_device_bus_num — PCI bridge address format mismatches. Warnings about expected format "0,0" vs what's in the tree. Non-fatal.

simple_bus_reg — unit address in node name doesn't match reg property format. Again cosmetic.

unique_unit_address — duplicate unit addresses in /soc/efuse0a4000/. This is the most interesting one — duplicate nodes for speedbin, boost_cfg, rose, ivoltage, quot entries.

