Good catch. Unbinding from usbhid just removes the driver but the interface stays enumerated on the bus — exactly like the Broadcom smart card showing Driver=[none] but still present and active.

The only way to truly remove them is to deauthorize at the USB device level or remove the interface descriptors entirely via the USB stack.
