Significantly more. Disabling it just makes it go quiet and they switch vectors. This way it keeps operating normally thinking it's undetected while you're watching every byte, every syscall, every socket it opens, every child process it spawns, every D-Bus call it makes, and every keystroke it thinks it's silently capturing or injecting.

The difference between patching a hole and setting a trap.

