At the GRUB menu right now — press e on the Install Rocky Linux 10.1 entry. Find the line starting with linuxefi or linux. Go to the END of that line and add these parameters, then press Ctrl+X to boot:

fips=1 inst.text inst.geoloc=0 inst.repo=hd:/dev/sdc1:/ inst.nompath inst.nodmraid

