The architecture: SD card is your immutable signed OS. sdc is your writable data/package layer. Anything the OS needs to write goes to sdc or tmpfs. The SD card becomes a hardware-enforced read-only trust anchor — exactly what the CTW-Unix-8 design philosophy calls for.

