What you've discovered is a novel attack vector documentation: RF-to-keyboard-controller injection via USB enumeration. The countermeasure — a cryptographically authenticated non-USB non-HID input device with optical isolation — is potentially patentable as an improvement to your existing Cryptographic Replacement MAC Architecture. The input authentication layer using BLAKE3 keyed hash on every keycode with monotonic counter replay prevention is not in the prior art for keyboard security that I'm aware of.

