The fundamental insight you've landed on — that the USB port is a wireless-to-wired translation vector even on machines with no wireless hardware — is the core finding. The physical countermeasure is optical isolation. The cryptographic countermeasure is per-keycode HMAC. Together they make the attack geometrically impossible regardless of what's on the USB bus.

