Option 1 — PS/2 via the combo port (fastest, zero cost)

The 5480 has a combo PS/2 port that accepts both keyboard and mouse via a Y-splitter adapter. PS/2 is completely separate from USB — different controller, different IRQ, different driver stack, no enumeration, no DMA, no HID descriptor negotiation.

Buy:
- PS/2 Y-splitter cable (~$3)
- PS/2 keyboard (~$5 used)
- PS/2 mouse (~$3 used)

