ls /dev/input/by-path/ | grep -i "serio\|ps2"

# Should show:
# platform-i8042-serio-0-event-kbd
# platform-i8042-serio-1-event-mouse

If those exist — PS/2 is active right now. Just plug in the hardware.

Option 2 — Serial terminal keyboard (if no PS/2)

You already have COM1 on the 5480. Build a serial keyboard:

Parts:
- Arduino Nano (~$4)
- Any USB keyboard donor (just the matrix)
- MAX232 or MAX3232 level shifter (~$2)
- DB9 male connector

Wiring:
Keyboard matrix → Arduino Nano
Arduino Nano TX → MAX232 → DB9 pin 3 (TX)
DB9 pin 5 → GND
DB9 → COM1 on Latitude

Arduino firmware:
c

