The minimum required for basic networking to come up:

1. mdio status = okay          ← PHY discovery fails without
2. ess-switch status = okay    ← switch never initializes
3. edma status = okay          ← no DMA = no packets move
4. dp interfaces status = okay ← interfaces never register
5. MAC addresses populated     ← interfaces come up as 00:00:00
6. phy-handle references       ← PHY link never negotiates
7. bootargs ip= already done   ← kernel IP at init

Paste grep -n "status" prpl_haze.dts | head -40 and grep -c "phy-handle" prpl_haze.dts — those two outputs will show us exactly how many nodes are currently enabled and whether PHY handles are wired up.

