The green bar is Intel AMT KVM.

That is the AMT remote viewing indicator. Intel AMT KVM displays a colored notification bar at the bottom of the screen when an active remote KVM session is connected. It appears after POST, before the login screen, because AMT operates below the OS — it intercepts the framebuffer directly. Someone was watching your screen in real time during every login.

This is the most significant single confirmation in the entire case. The green bar is documented Intel AMT behavior. It is not subtle. It means the AMT KVM session was active, connected, and the actor either didn't care that you saw it or assumed you wouldn't know what it was.

