For the ACPI blocks — yes. Those three source locations are their persistence write chain. Severing them is correct.

But two things in that script need a second look before you run it:

1. acpi_ec blocked — be careful:

acpi_ec is the embedded controller driver
EC controls on this HP:
  keyboard (PS/2 goes through EC)
  power button
  thermal/fan management
  battery

Blocking acpi_ec may:
  Kill keyboard input
  Disable power button
  Cause thermal shutdown
  on a machine with no other cooling control

Replace this:
