What this covers:

prerouting (-400):
  Bogons, fragments, bad TCP flags
  IP options, ICMP redirect, RH0
  IPv6 extension header abuse
  Hits before anything else

input:
  Default DROP policy
  SYN flood with dynamic IP tracking
  SSH LAN-only rate limited 3/min
  AMT all ports blocked
  Dangerous port set blocked
  NDP flood protection
  Everything else logged and dropped

forward:
  Hard DROP — not a router

output:
  AMT outbound blocked (ME cant phone home)
  sssd C2 ports blocked (LDAP/Kerberos)
  Plain DNS blocked (force encrypted)
  Bogon destinations blocked

IPv4 specific:
  Martians, localhost spoofing, SSRF

IPv6 specific:
  Unsolicited NA (NDP spoofing)
  Fragmented NDP packets

Paste nft -c -f /etc/nftables.conf result — zero errors means it loads clean and we're ready to go online hardened.

