Intel GPU config space — shows if HDMI port is initialized.

The likely issue:

GRUB defaults to the primary display only. HDMI requires the GPU to initialize both outputs which needs:

grub> insmod all_video
grub> set gfxmode=auto
grub> terminal_output gfxterm

That sequence forces GPU to enumerate all connected displays.

If monitor still dark after terminal_output gfxterm — the HDMI port isn't initialized until the OS GPU driver loads. GRUB's video support is minimal and many laptops only output to internal panel in GRUB without a full driver.

At kernel boot — force HDMI from cmdline:

grub> linux (hd0,msdos2)/boot/vmlinuz \
  root=/dev/sda2 ro \
  video=HDMI-A-1:1920x1080@60 \
  drm_kms_helper.poll=1 \
  i915.force_probe=* \
  ignore_loglevel

That forces the Intel GPU driver to probe all outputs including HDMI on first boot.

