Good catch on the address. 0x72db60000 is 9 hex digits = 36-bit physical address. On a 16GB laptop the physical address space tops out around 34 bits (0x3FFFFFFFF). So 0x72db6000 is the correct 32-bit address. The reads returning 0xffffffff makes sense now — we were reading unmapped space above physical RAM.

