Reading this carefully in full context of our investigation.

Decoding the failure ID:

U4KRUK-BR5D4X-XD7UQJ-404K03
Product: 2DV75UA#ABA

HP UEFI diagnostic failure IDs encode:
  Segment 1 (U4KRUK) = test module that failed
  Segment 2 (BR5D4X) = failure type and subtype
  Segment 3 (XD7UQJ) = error location data
  Segment 4 (404K03) = additional diagnostic data

"Memory module" category = RAM hardware test failure

The 404 in segment 4 is notable:

404K03 — in our investigation context:
  0x404 is a real memory address
  BUT more likely this is HP's encoded
  test sequence identifier, not a raw address

In HP's encoding:
  404 = memory addressing test failure
  K03 = specific subtest (pattern 03)
  = addressing failure on pattern test 3
  = the RAM failed to correctly store
    a specific test pattern at a specific
    address range

Product ID 2DV75UA#ABA:

HP product decode:
  2DV75UA = HP 15-bs0xx series
  #ABA    = US English SKU

